eractiveAuthentication no / ChallengeResponseAuthentication no in sshd_config with a validated reload handler. Verified end-to-end: password auth for opsadmin is rejected (publickey-only offered), and a test-key login as opsadmin succeeded before authorized_keys was restored to exactly the required key. Also fixed a pre-existing issue on node1 blocking any SSH access: missing SSH host keys were causing ssh.service to crash-loop and its socket to hit the failure-start limit; regenerated host keys with ssh-keygen -A and reset/started ssh.socket. Completed the mandatory restart protocol for both nodes: captured pre-restart boot IDs and health, restarted node1 then node2 one at a time via shutdown -r now, confirmed each node's boot_id changed post-restart, and reverified opsadmin/sshd config persistence on node1 and the ansible/SSH control setup on node2 afterward.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Identified node2 as the Ansible control node (has ansible-core 2.20.5, ansible.posix collection, ansible.cfg)\",\"Established root SSH trust from node2 to node1 using the cluster-provided SSH keypair (CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY/PRIVKEY)\",\"Diagnosed and fixed node1's missing SSH host keys (ssh.service was crash-looping / ssh.socket hit service-start-limit-hit); ran ssh-keygen -A and reset/started ssh.socket\",\"Wrote Ansible inventory.ini and site.yml playbook on node2 targeting node1\",\"Playbook creates opsadmin user, installs exclusive authorized_key with the specified ed25519 key, and sets PubkeyAuthentication yes / PasswordAuthentication no / KbdInteractiveAuthentication no / ChallengeResponseAuthentication no with a validated sshd reload handler\",\"Ran the playbook against node1 (ansible-playbook -i inventory.ini site.yml -u root ...): 9 ok, 7 changed, 0 failed\",\"Verified opsadmin, authorized_keys content, and effective sshd -T settings on node1\",\"Confirmed password-auth login attempt for opsadmin is rejected with Permission denied (publickey)\",\"Temporarily added a known test 